Meanwhile at the same time just across the border in Naboisho most of the=
 Ikisiausiau breakaway pride (25 in number) were perhaps unwisely taking o=
n another  large bull=2C this time uninjured.

There were several lively rounds but this was a seasoned heavyweight v cal=
low bantamweights with only really one outcome particularly as most of the=
 pride preferred the view from the gallery.

http://www.kicheche.com/kicheche-valley/?utm_source=3DRACK+-+agents+SOW&ut=
m_campaign=3D5253ea3d8a-Spot+of+the+Week+-+Bufffalo+Soldiers_COPY_04&utm_m=
edium=3Demail&utm_term=3D0_-b983f9deb7-33796176

A day later Johnson and Bernard watched a formidable lion coalition drop a=
 buffalo cow. They had begun feasting when a large male charcoal ruminant=
 appeared and savagely interrupted their meal.

This was suddenly a serious confrontation=2C with no thought of the buffal=
o winging it (sorry) and before long the cats retreated unimpressed by thi=
s bull****=2C and=2C miraculously the cow ( now christened Lazarus) rose=
=2C albeit unsteadily=2C above the oat grass..
